1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,644
In Cebu City, devotees light candles
before a small image of the Child Jesus.

2
00:00:05,644 --> 00:00:09,390
Its recorded story begins more than five
centuries ago.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:17,053
On April 7, 1521, Magellan’s expedition
arrived in Cebu, then known as Sugbo,

4
00:00:17,053 --> 00:00:19,300
where Rajah Humabon ruled.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,093
One week later, on April 14, Humabon and
his wife were baptized.

6
00:00:25,093 --> 00:00:27,880
She received the Christian name Juana.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:35,498
Antonio Pigafetta, the expedition’s
chronicler, recorded that Juana received

8
00:00:35,498 --> 00:00:39,590
an image of the Child Jesus, known in Cebu
as the Santo Niño.

9
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:46,858
Forty-four years later, on April 28, 1565,
Legazpi’s expedition reached Cebu.

10
00:00:46,858 --> 00:00:49,710
Its ships fired on the settlement.

11
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:56,611
A sailor named Juan Camus found the
statuette in a dwelling, identified as the

12
00:00:56,611 --> 00:00:58,920
image given to Juana in 1521.

13
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,079
Augustinian friars took custody of the
image.

14
00:01:03,079 --> 00:01:07,778
A church and convent rose at the site of
the discovery, where the Basilica now

15
00:01:07,778 --> 00:01:08,200
stands.

16
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,388
Generations of pilgrims come to Cebu to
honor the Child Jesus.

17
00:01:14,388 --> 00:01:19,470
During Fiesta Señor, they join novena
Masses and carry his image in procession.

18
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:24,634
The devotion spread through parish
celebrations and family prayer.

19
00:01:24,634 --> 00:01:28,740
In many homes, the Santo Niño found a
place on the family altar.

20
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,054
Filipinos carried the devotion overseas.

21
00:01:33,054 --> 00:01:38,613
In new communities, families and parishes
kept it alive through novenas, Masses and

22
00:01:38,613 --> 00:01:40,020
feast-day gatherings.

23
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:45,080
The Cebu confraternity established
chapters abroad, including Indonesia,

24
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,160
Singapore and the United States.

25
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:50,250
In 2023, a Vatican City chapter was
inaugurated.

26
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,718
On October 17, fifty members of the
Filipino Santo Niño community were

27
00:01:54,718 --> 00:01:58,420
welcomed into the confraternity at the
Church of Saint Anne.

28
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:06,253
From Cebu to Filipino communities
worldwide, devotees still honor Jesus as

29
00:02:06,253 --> 00:02:07,439
the Holy Child.

30
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:09,160
Viva Señor Santo Niño!

